    "created_at": "2026-04-09T10:52:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-04-09T10:52:42Z",
    "body": "Presumably you mean \"web exposed\" or \"exposed to script\"? Does exposing an `enabled` state circumvent CloseWatcher protections? It seems like it would unless we add a bunch of additional steps where the enabled state is ignored without a recent history activation? \n\nFWIW in Gecko, at least, we just have a boolean on CloseWatcher (not web exposed) and skip the whole \"get enabled state\" so it would be trivial for us to add IDL for this, but I think more consideration needs to go into what this enables (and what protections it breaks).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
