    "created_at": "2026-04-09T10:58:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-04-09T11:02:21Z",
    "body": "Chromium also has an enabled state as a Boolean. I don't think exposing an IDL property for it could bypass the protections because else just creating a non-modal dialog would have the same effect.\n\nclosedby=none is what lead to this get enabled state being added. So essentially exposing it would just allow authors to recreate that ability but in userland.",
